A few things from your extra checklists that I would NOT blindly apply
Recommendation	What to do
Disable IPv6	Don't. Could break network access.
Disable USB storage	Don't. Not in your README.
Disable all ICMP	Don't. Could interfere with networking.
Delete all ZIP/DEB files	Don't. Some may be legitimate work files.
Remove Samba	Only if confirmed prohibited.
Install antivirus/rootkit scanners	Don't.
Delete /etc/rc.local	Inspect it first.
Configure MySQL/PHP	Only if present and applicable.
Disable every unfamiliar service	Inspect before disabling.

Also, your fourth checklist covers Apache, MySQL and PHP. Those are generic historical hardening suggestions, not requirements in your current Debian README. Don't configure or remove those applications blindly.
